WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.135 --> 00:00:03.691
- Coming home, I think the best part

00:00:03.691 --> 00:00:05.920
was seeing my family and friends.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.325
And feeling this immense love and pride

00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:11.331
and just feeling great to see them

00:00:11.331 --> 00:00:14.350
and then just walking on
terra firma again, you know?

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:17.896
Not floating around but just
feeling the Earth beneath you,

00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:19.553
that's a beautiful moment.

00:00:19.553 --> 00:00:22.422
(light ethereal music)

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.662
I had those moments of, "Where am I?

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:26.780
"Am I in space, am I at
home, am I on the ground,

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.407
"how am I gonna move, how am I gonna eat?

00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:32.581
"Am I able to throw food in
the air and go fly and get it?"

00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:36.699
To walk on the beach was just
the most incredible thing.

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:38.414
When you look at the horizon,

00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:41.644
it kind of helps regauge
your gyros in your inner ears

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:44.009
and it helps know exactly
what's up and down

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.592
and right and left.

00:00:47.376 --> 00:00:51.483
Driving felt interesting
because you've been traveling

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:54.070
at 17,500 miles per hour.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.503
And then you come back
and you get in your car

00:00:55.503 --> 00:00:58.286
and you're like, "Oh, I'm
going 60 miles an hour, huh?”

00:00:58.286 --> 00:00:59.124
"That's nothing.”

00:00:59.124 --> 00:00:59.957
"I'm going a hundred miles an hour.”

00:00:59.957 --> 00:01:01.530
"Oh, that's nothing."

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.947
It changes the way you think about speed.

00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:08.281
I think food tasted better.

00:01:08.281 --> 00:01:10.728
After eating the rehydrated vegetables

00:01:10.728 --> 00:01:13.027
and the irradiated turkey,

00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:16.573
coming home to a wonderful
meal and sharing it

00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:18.448
and not having to go chase it

00:01:18.448 --> 00:01:21.285
when it bounces off or
something, and you can pick it up

00:01:21.285 --> 00:01:25.452
and you know it's coming to
your mouth, that's pretty cool.

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:32.102
If you wanna go to space, it
would be one of these things

00:01:32.102 --> 00:01:36.072
that is transformative on
so many different levels.

00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:37.594
I would tell future explorers

00:01:37.594 --> 00:01:40.862
to make sure that when
you worked with others

00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:42.804
that you work as a team,

00:01:42.804 --> 00:01:46.971
you see all people as potential,
you know, space travelers together,

00:01:47.946 --> 00:01:49.388
no matter what language they speak,

00:01:49.388 --> 00:01:51.900
no matter what they look like,
no matter what food they eat,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.236
and to know that we're
all in this together

00:01:54.236 --> 00:01:56.903
and work hard and share the fun.

